Kind: ablation
Issue: #771
Takes out: the switch's use of the continuation -- every thread resumes by returning through the frames it blocked in, as this target did before #771; a thread that blocked with one then carries its continuation over saved frames, which the check on the way back in names, and on a kernel without that check -Q's fourth arm sees thread_block() come back
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 25 1200 -smp 1
Expect: (switch_context: thread [^ ]+ resumes in frames it saved, and its continuation field says|handoff: WRONG — a thread that blocked with a continuation came back from thread_block)

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/machine.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/machine.c
index aead184e..0728b44b 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/machine.c
